  "worked_solution": "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\u27e8\\operatorname{cos}\u20613t,0,-\\operatorname{sin}\u20613t\u27e9\\times \u27e8-\\operatorname{sin}\u20613t,0,-\\operatorname{cos}\u20613t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}\u20613t & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}\u20613t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}\u20613t & 0 & -\\operatorname{cos}\u20613t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =[\\text{\u00a0}\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & -\\operatorname{sin}\u20613t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{cos}\u20613t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u20613t & -\\operatorname{sin}\u20613t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}\u20613t & -\\operatorname{cos}\u20613t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u20613t & 0 \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}\u20613t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{\u00a0}] \\\\  & =\u27e80-0,-(-{cos}^{2}\u20613t-{sin}^{2}\u20613t),0-0\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,1,0\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
